Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

## What this PR introduces

### Domain Layer
- BranchInventoryRequest entity (new aggregate)
- BranchInventoryRequestStatus enum (Pending / Approved / Rejected / Fulfilled)
- Product.CriticalStockThreshold (nullable int, per-product low-stock threshold)

### Application Layer
- IInventoryNotificationService interface (transport-agnostic, implemented in Phase 5)
- LowStockDetectedNotification (MediatR INotification)
- LargeInventoryRequestedNotification (MediatR INotification)
- InventoryNotificationOptions (strongly-typed config, bound from appsettings.json)
- Full CQRS slice for BranchInventoryRequest:
  - CreateBranchInventoryRequestCommand
  - CreateBranchInventoryRequestCommandValidator
  - CreateBranchInventoryRequestCommandHandler
  - BranchInventoryRequestDto
- StartTransferCommandHandler: publishes LowStockDetectedNotification after stock deduction
- CompleteTransferCommandHandler: publishes LowStockDetectedNotification after completion

### Infrastructure Layer
- BranchInventoryRequestConfiguration (EF Core Fluent API)
- ProductConfiguration: added CriticalStockThreshold column mapping
- DatabaseContext: added BranchInventoryRequests DbSet
- Migration: AddBranchInventoryRequestsAndCriticalStockThreshold

### WebAPI Layer
- BranchInventoryRequestsController (POST endpoint)
- appsettings.json: InventoryNotifications section with LargeRequestThreshold
- Program.cs: passes IConfiguration to AddApplicationLayer
- AddApplicationLayer signature updated to accept IConfiguration

## Architecture notes
- No SignalR yet — notification handlers will be added in Phase 5
- LowStockDetectedNotification publishes with empty WarehouseManagerUserId;
  user resolution will be implemented in Phase 5 (known limitation)
- All Clean Architecture boundaries respected
- No business logic in controllers or infrastructure
